JITTERBUG NETWORK TOPOLOGY
A strategy for sparse network resiliency
Foundational public statement: 26 November 2026

Om Design identifies this publication as the originator's account of Jitterbug Network Topology: an autonomous, adaptive approach to sparse network resiliency in which communication difficulties can stimulate local structural expansion, followed by contraction that retains useful connection experience.

Public access is intended to invite independent scholarly discussion, criticism, and properly attributed citation. Please credit Om Design, the work's title, and the relevant dated version or commit when citing this work.

